{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Program Files\\\\PowerShell\\\\7\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"Get-Content -Raw 'C:/Projects/ai-template.wt/review-tmp/2026-11-02b-leg30/spine-change-list.md'; Get-ChildItem docs/reviews/wi-978 -File | Select-Object -ExpandProperty FullName | ForEach-Object { \\\"\"'`n--- $_\"; Get-Content -Raw $_ }; git diff --no-ext-diff --stat 2f4ebb2a5..HEAD; git diff --no-ext-diff 2f4ebb2a5..HEAD -- docs/requirements/system-requirements.toml docs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml docs/requirements/interfaces.toml docs/test/test-cases.toml'","aggregated_output":"# WI-978 spine change list (stage 1, the tests)\n\nNo registry was edited. Proposed changes, for the coordinator and the P15 reconciliation:\n\n1. TC-402 `evidence` (Drafted): add the landing-table cases the row's method drives (\"Drive every\n   landing-table outcome ... on both callers\") but its evidence cell does not name:\n   - `tests/test_id_landing.py::test_the_slot_refuses_each_unreserved_landing` (5 params: no-record,\n     another-wis-record, retired-number, no-carrier, landing-only-record)\n   - `tests/test_id_landing.py::test_the_slot_rung_refuses_ids_added_under_an_unreadable_claim`\n   - `tests/test_id_landing.py::test_the_slot_lands_a_lane_whose_ids_sit_in_its_own_record`\n     (characterization, row 2 at the slot)\n   - `tests/test_id_landing.py::test_a_code_only_lane_with_no_carrier_lands` (characterization,\n     row 1 at the slot)\n   - `tests/test_id_landing.py::test_a_watermark_conflict_beside_another_conflict_still_refuses`\n     (characterization, the plan's P7 refresh guard)\n   - `tests/test_id_landing.py::test_the_hand_squash_refuses_each_unreserved_landing` (5 params)\n   - `tests/test_id_landing.py::test_the_hand_squash_passes_ids_in_its_own_record`\n   - `tests/test_id_landing.py::test_the_hand_squash_refuses_ids_added_under_an_unreadable_claim`\n2. TC-158 `evidence` (Approved; amended in this lane's intent set): two tests not in the cell,\n   proposed for addition at the checkpoint (or left out, the coordinator's call):\n   - `tests/test_id_watermark.py::test_an_unchanged_committed_baseline_passes_the_floor` (the\n     control for the git-baseline cases)\n   - `tests/test_id_watermark.py::test_the_live_id_finding_points_a_lane_at_the_reserve_verb` (the\n     plan's P4 text change: the live-id finding names `--reserve-ids`)\n3. LLR-363 `code_symbol` (binds at P15): the tests fix two trace seams the cell does not list,\n   `live_ids` and `live_ids_at` (the one live-id sweep, over the working tree and over a git tree).\n4. LLR-362 `code_symbol` (binds at P15): the tests use `Refused` (the one refusal type of the\n   argument parsers); the plan's P4 also names `record_history_findings`, which no test calls\n   directly (it is driven through the CLI).\n\nNo test is named differently from a name a row already gives: every evidence entry in TC-158,\nTC-401 and TC-402 exists under that exact name.\n\n\n# Stage 2 (P2 to P5, the carrier code) additions\n\nNo registry was edited. Names the code built that the intent rows do not give (for the P15\nreconciliation; each binds there):\n\n5. LLR-362 `code_symbol`: the built names beyond the cell's list.\n   - In `project-trajectory/scripts/id_carrier.py`: `WATERMARK`, `MAX_COUNT`, `LOST_RACE`,\n     `RESERVE_VERB`, `CORRECTION_LINE`, `Refused` (an alias of `ValueError`, see 7),\n     `parse_marks`, `parse_corrections` (moved from trace.py, see 6), `record_line`, `reserve`\n     (the reservation's orchestration: argument checks, the trunk claim, the plan, the carrier\n     write), `receiving_sides` (the receiving file's sides, stages 2 and 3 when conflicted),\n     `record_history_findings` (the committed-record union check). Private helpers: `_count`,\n     `_ref_value`, `_plumb`, `_claimed`, `_id_name`, `_outside_lines`.\n   - In `project-trajectory/scripts/trace.py`: `reserve_ids` (the `--reserve-ids` verb's library\n     call; IF-101's `data` already names it), `committed_reservations`, `_baseline_texts` (the one\n     parent walk the three committed readers share), `_reserved_highs`, `_basis`,\n     `_render_full`, `_trunk_name`, `_committed_marks` (was `_watermark_at`, now over a text the shared walk\n     reads), `_cmd_reserve_ids`, `_cmd_fold_ids`; `watermark_findings` gains a\n     `previous_reservations` argument. `parse_corrections` stays a trace name (an alias of the\n     moved reader).\n6. LLR-362 `module`/`code_symbol`: `parse_corrections` (and the correction-line grammar) moved\n   from trace.py into id_carrier.py, because the fold unions correction records over texts and\n   must read them with the one grammar; trace.py keeps `parse_corrections` as an alias, so no\n   caller changed. Not the S5 \"move the watermark section\" refactor: only the line grammars the\n   fold reads moved.\n7. LLR-362: `Refused` is `ValueError` itself, not a subclass. `tests/test_id_carrier.py` loads the\n   module afresh for every symbol it reads (`_ic()` per `_sym` call), so a class defined in the\n   module is a different class per load and `pytest.raises(<load A's Refused>)` misses load B's\n   raise. Proposed: either keep the alias (as built) or change the test to load the module once,\n   then restore a dedicated subclass.\n8. IF-101 `data` names the fold verb as `fold_ids`; the built library call is `fold_watermark`\n   (the name LLR-363's `code_symbol` already gives) and the CLI flag is `--fold-ids`. Proposed:\n   IF-101 `data` reads `fold_watermark` (or keeps `fold_ids` as the verb's name; the coordinator's\n   call).\n9. `project-trajectory/scripts/kitlib/git.py` `git_bytes` gains an optional `stdin` (bytes, fed\n   untranslated): the carrier's `hash-object --stdin` and `mktree` input must not have its\n   newlines turned into CRLF on Windows, which `git_out`'s text-mode `stdin` does. Its owning\n   rows (the kitlib git seam) are outside this spec's named surface; no row cell names the\n   argument list, so no cell change is proposed, only noted.\n10. IF-224 `data` (Drafted; owner `scripts/agent_common`, requestor `scripts/trace`): the\n    reservation reads the declared trunk's name through `agent_common.trunk_name`, from\n    `trace._trunk_name` (a deferred import, the same edge IF-224 declares), so the claim check\n    asks the kit's one trunk reader. IF-224's `data` names only `human_approves_spine`.\n    Proposed: IF-224 `data` gains \"trunk_name(root) -> the declared trunk's name, or raises\n    TrunkUndeclared\" (or IF-179, which already states `trunk_name`, gains `scripts/trace` as a\n    requestor; the coordinator's call). The first build placed the read in `id_carrier`, which\n    made a new CMP-006 -> CMP-008 edge with no seam (`check_trajectory --strict` ERROR) and a new\n    deferred import edge (`tests/test_import_layers.py`'s stamped window); moving it to trace\n    reuses the declared edge and leaves both green.\n\n\n# Stage 3 (P6 to P9, the landing) additions\n\nNo registry was edited. Names the code built that the intent rows do not give (for the P15\nreconciliation; each binds there):\n\n11. LLR-363 `code_symbol`: the built names beyond the cell's list. In\n    `project-trajectory/scripts/trace.py`: `live_ids` (the one live-id sweep, `live_max_ids` now\n    derives from it), `live_ids_at` (the sweep at a git tree). In\n    `project-trajectory/scripts/integrate.py`: `_fold_watermark_conflict` (a refresh conflict on\n    the watermark settled by the fold), `_fold_carrier_in` (the refresh's carrier fold after\n    merging trunk in), `WATERMARK`; `_merge_refusal` gains the rung (already a symbol of other\n    rows), `integrate_one` calls `_landing_ready`. In `project-trajectory/scripts/check.py`:\n    `_reserved_ids_refusal` (the step's judgement), `_squash_work_items` (the squashed lane's\n    claim read), `FOLD_REMEDY`; `_reserved_ids_mode` is in the cell already.\n12. LLR-363 `module`: the shipped `project-trajectory/hooks/pre