ds, so the rung passes the lane on to the rung the\n    test measures.\n    - `tests/test_integrate_admission.py::test_a_lane_that_mints_a_row_born_approved_is_refused`\n      (SR 2-2 for WI-401); its TC's evidence cell is unchanged.\n    - `tests/test_held_status_git.py::test_an_off_spine_demotion_and_a_born_Drafted_row_land_from_a_loop_lane`\n      (B 3-3 for WI-401).\n\n\n# Stage 4 (P10 to P13, the text) additions\n\nNo registry was edited.\n\n18. The landing judgement checks its sixth table row (a landing watermark record that neither\n    the carrier nor the parent holds) only when the landing adds carrier-space ids:\n    `id_carrier.landing_lines` returns at once when nothing is added. The spec's table lists the\n    row on its own; the built code reads row 1 (\"no carrier-space id added: passes\") first. The\n    stage-4 texts (trace.py's IF-101 header, runtime flow 9, the RESYNC entry) state the built\n    behaviour. If LLR-363's or TC-402's wording reads the row as unconditional, it either gains\n    \"when ids are added\" at the reconcile, or the code changes in a later stage (not done here:\n    this stage changes no behaviour).\n19. TC-402 or a coordinator-text TC (none exists; the coordinator tooling is outside the\n    component map): the new pins in `tests/test_prompts.py`,\n    `test_the_terra_brief_drafts_new_ids_only_from_its_reserved_ranges` and\n    `test_the_cycle_reserves_before_drafting_and_folds_the_watermark` (3 params), verify the\n    procedure text only. No row is proposed to cite them; noted for the coordinator.\n\n\n# Fix round 1 (the 6701eec reviews) additions\n\nNo registry was edited.\n\n20. TC-402 `evidence` (Drafted): add three regression tests in `tests/test_id_landing.py`:\n    - `test_a_registry_an_export_ignore_rule_hides_is_still_judged` (the judgement at a lane tip\n      and the hand squash's `reserved-ids` step, with a committed `export-ignore` rule over the\n      registries);\n    - `test_the_slot_refuses_an_unreserved_id