efore a trunk mint it is what makes the folded file committable. The fold\n    lag reads the same contribution.\n25. LLR-363: the refresh folds a watermark conflict only when it is the sole conflicted path\n    (its detail already says \"a refresh conflict limited to the watermark resolves to that fold;\n    any other conflict remains refused\"; no cell change proposed).\n26. `retire.py` now imports `id_carrier` (an intra-CMP-006 edge; `retire.read_marks` reads through\n    `id_carrier.parse_marks`). LLR-286's `code_symbol` does not list `read_marks`; no cell\n    change proposed.\n\n\n# Fix round 2 (the e5ecf9d reviews) additions\n\nNo registry was edited.\n\n27. TC-402 `evidence` (Drafted): add the slot regression test\n    `tests/test_id_landing.py::test_the_slot_lands_a_code_only_lane_after_trunk_deletes_an_id_it_based_on`\n    (a code-only lane whose base holds an id trunk then deletes lands through the merge slot,\n    unrefreshed; it failed on the pre-fix rung, which compared the tip with trunk's tip).\n    TC-402's `method` may want \"and a code-only lane after trunk retired an id from its base\"\n    beside \"a stale-base lane that minted another lane's reserved number\".\n28. LLR-363 `detail` (Drafted), for the checkpoint's reading: \"added\" at the automated landing is\n    over the lane's base (its merge base with trunk, the delta the mint rung reads); at the hand\n    landing it is over HEAD (git's squash is already merged onto it). The cell says neither \"parent\"\n    nor \"base\", so no change is required; if the sitting wants the reading stated, \"an identity\n    the landing adds over the tree its change is made on\" covers both routes. LLR-363\n    `code_symbol` gains `_lane_base` (integrate.py; the R1 mint rung shares it).\n29. LLR-362 `code_symbol`: `check_work_item` is unchanged as a name but now lives in trace.py\n    (already in the row's module cell): it reads the reserve verb's argument through the kit's one\n    lane-input parser, `agent_common.parse_wi_id`. `id_carrier.reserve` takes the checked id;\n    `id_carrier._claimed` is deleted.\n30. IF-224 `data` (Drafted; extends item 10): the tracer's deferred `agent_common` import now also\n    reads `parse_wi_id(value, source) -> the one WI id, or raises ValueError` for the reserve\n    verb's work-item check (IF-179 gaining `scripts/trace`, if that row already states the parser,\n    is the alternative; the coordinator's call).\n31. LLR-141 (Approved; `kitlib/git.py` in its module cell, `claimed_work_branch` in its\n    `code_symbol`) `code_symbol`: the one claim-folder reader at a tree-ish, `claimed_specs`, with\n    its grammar `SPEC_NAME` and folder `ACTIVE_DIR`, tagged `Implements: SR-170, LLR-141`, beside\n    `claimed_work_branch`. Its callers: `check._squash_work_items` and `id_carrier.reserve`;\n    `integrate._spec_id` reads `SPEC_NAME`. Proposed: append them to LLR-141's cell at the next\n    sitting that touches it, or name a different home.\n32. LLR-181 `code_symbol` (items 14 and 23): `extract_paths` is withdrawn, its body back in\n    `rejudge._archive_chunk` as at the lane base (rejudge.py is unchanged over the base);\n    `ArchiveError`, `write_blobs` and `_listed_blobs` remain the landing's tree read.\n33. TC-401 `evidence` (Drafted), optional: `tests/test_id_carrier_git.py::test_the_claim_folder_reader_reads_each_lanes_work_items_at_a_revision`\n    (the reader the reserve verb's claim check and the hand squash share).\n\n\n# Fix round 3 (the 6f02ab8 reviews and dispute sitting 008) additions\n\nNo registry was edited.\n\n34. LLR-363 `detail` (Drafted; the sitting's amendment, through its own authority): the landing\n    refuses an added identity that a retirement record in the landing tree or its parent names,\n    inside the work item's reservation as well as outside it, naming the identity and the record;\n    range membership authorizes only a number not yet retired. Proposed sentence for the detail:\n    \"An added identity that