fold_watermark` for `fold_ids`): the owner contract in trace.py now states that\n    `landing_id_refusal(root, landing_rev, parent_rev, wi_ids, claim_source, lane=None)` also reads\n    the lane tip's delta over its merge base and the retirement records. A short Data proposal:\n    \"read_watermark, bump_watermark, reserve_ids, fold_watermark, landing_id_refusal, landing_fold_lag\n    over docs/id-watermark and the id carrier ref\" (contract detail stays in trace.py).\n37. IF-257 `data` (Drafted): the retirement records gain a reader at a git tree,\n    `retire.recorded_at(root, rev) -> {(space, number): relpath}` (record files by name, readable\n    or not), read by `scripts/trace` (already a consumer) for the landing check. The cell\n    describes the files only, so no change is required; the contract text in retire.py names the\n    call. LLR-286 `code_symbol` (retire.py) gains `recorded_at` (tagged `Implements: SR-226,\n    LLR-286`: one module owns every question asked of the records, per LLR-286's rationale).\n38. LLR-362 / LLR-363 `code_symbol` (with 005-REVIEW-A F3 / 006-REVIEW-B F3's re-tag): the new\n    id_carrier functions `_retired_lines` and `_read_landing` carry `Implements: SR-174, LLR-362`\n    like their landing siblings (LLR-363's module cell lacks id_carrier.py today); at the re-tag\n    they move with `landing_lines`, `landing_refusal`, `_outside_lines`, `_added_ids`, `ids_at` to\n    LLR-363.\n39. IF-173 (Drafted; data cell unchanged, \"seven _-prefixed readers\" still true): the dispatcher\n    now takes `_landing_ready` in place of `_merge_ready`; integrate.py's IF-173 contract text says\n    so. LLR-363 `code_symbol` already lists `_landing_ready`.\n\r\n\n--- C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-978\\docs\\reviews\\wi-978\\001-REVIEW-A-6701eec.md\r\nReviewed: 6701eec3831f5b3b5d18a61a765caa52dc540768\n\nVerified: Independently reviewed the prescribed three-dot diff, WI-978 and its item-16 spec target/quoted owner ruling, PROCESS sections 3–6, the