ngled ref list) and asserts each is REFUSED with a finding naming the row and field, so the clean result is evidence rather than a check that cannot fail.\"\"\"\ndocs/test/test-cases.toml-1616-tier = \"Smoke\"\ndocs/test/test-cases.toml-1617-expected = \"Satisfies SR-147 AcceptanceCriteria\"\n--\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml:1391:[design.LLR-141]\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-1392-sr_refs = [\"SR-006\", \"SR-170\"]\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-1393-title = \"Work-branch lane signal + freshness skip\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-1394-module = \"project-trajectory/scripts/check.py;project-trajectory/scripts/kitlib/git.py\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-1395-code_symbol = \"_claimed_work_branch/_implausible_branch_notice/steps/claimed_work_branch\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-1396-detail = \"\"\"On a claimed work branch the _TRUNK_FRESHNESS_STEPS set SKIPs with a §5.2 notice, exit code untouched; the plan listing still names every step. The claim signal answers in two stages - docs/work/active/<branch>/ on disk (the fast path), else the branch's own committed history (git log -1 -- docs/work/active/<branch>) - so the closing commit that archives the claim, and every commit after it, keep the skip. No git, a failing git, or an empty answer all read as the trunk lane: a false work-branch positive would switch the freshness gates off on the one branch that owns regenerating them.\"\"\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-1397-rationale = \"\"\"A false work-branch positive would relax the trunk's freshness bar, so every ambiguity resolves toward the trunk lane.\"\"\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-1398-test_refs = \"(see TC-134)\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-1399-status = \"Approved\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-1400-component = \"CMP-007\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-1401-phase = 4\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-1402-\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-1403-[design.LLR-142]\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-1404-sr_refs = [\"SR-173\"]\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-1405-title = \"Trunk-step artifact regen (dependency order)\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-1406-module = \"project-trajectory/scripts/trunk_step.py\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-1407-code_symbol = \"regen\"\n--\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml:1870:[design.LLR-181]\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-1871-sr_refs = [\"SR-166\"]\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-1872-title = \"The shared helper package, and its complete arrival in a scaffold\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-1873-module = \"project-trajectory/scripts/kitlib/__init__.py;project-trajectory/scripts/kitlib/config.py;project-trajectory/scripts/kitlib/git.py;project-trajectory/scripts/kitlib/registry.py\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-1874-code_symbol = \"first_declared_line/read_spec_rows/git_out/read_toml_text/adjudicates_tokens/plan_table_rows/_table_cells/_plan_header\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-1875-detail = \"kitlib is the kit's one home for behaviours that were previously copied per script: config.first_declared_line with its two adapters (read_declared substituting a caller default, read_declared_lower lowercasing to a \\\"\\\" sentinel), registry's docs/work/ spec-folder reader (the row shape, the frontmatter/status/body parse and the ordered read), and git.git_out, the best-effort-off-git subprocess pattern that answers None on any failure and leaves the fail-direction to its caller. registry.adjudicates_tokens is the one raw scope-cell reader: the cell is absent or a TOML list of non-empty, semicolon-free strings after trimming; every other shape is refused without coercion by both the route and merge readers. Themed modules, never one generic common file. Every module of the package is a bootstrap.MAPPING row, so a scaffold receives it whole; bootstrap.py imports it and imports no other sibling, and the package imports no sibling at all. The completeness of that manifest is asked of a REAL SCAFFOLD, not of this repo, because this repo's scripts/ holds every file and a partial copy would read green here and ImportError on an adopter's first check.\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-1876-rationale = \"\"\"Owner ruling D-8 (OI-16, inversion confirmed 2026-08-13) replaced the F5 rule, under which a shared module was rejected so each script stayed independently copy-able. F5 bounded nothing: a 2026-08-12 census found the declared-line reader with five homes carrying a false claim of equivalence, is_example with three homes one of which crashed on None, and a 270-line spec-folder reader copied verbatim into three modules — a copy that had itself drifted by the time this row landed. Equality pins could contain that class but never shrink it. The INVERSION is the load-bearing half: D-8's literal step 2 (import from bootstrap.py) is unbuildable because bootstrap.py is deliberately absent from its own MAPPING, so a shipped script importing it would raise ModuleNotFoundError on a fresh scaffold while passing in the kit — the exact failure this repo shipped once when MAPPING omitted schedule.py. So the package ships like any other sibling and the scaffolder imports FROM it. The four-component tag was never a claim that four units own one behaviour — the package is imported from every component, and which unit OWNS a shared kernel was a partition question the locked depth-0 frame did not answer on its own; that question has since resolved to ONE owning component, CMP-006, the recorded closest-fit reason being registry.py's bulk within this row's own module set (304 of 572 lines, the four files above). The four-way tag collapses to that one component; the package's cross-component consumption does not disappear, it moves to a declared shared-kernel surface (docs/kernel-modules-allow) — a per-entry recorded declaration, never a bare tag, and never special-cased to kitlib.\"\"\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-1877-test_refs = \"TC-176; TC-331\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-1878-status = \"Approved\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-1879-component = \"CMP-006\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-1880-phase = 5\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-1881-\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-1882-[design.LLR-182]\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-1883-sr_refs = [\"SR-144\"]\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-1884-title = \"The lane-close terminal-outcome vocabulary, one home below its readers\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-1885-module = \"project-trajectory/scripts/kitlib/station.py\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-1886-code_symbol = \"Outcome/OUTCOME_DIRS/outcome_of\"\n--\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml:3383:[design.LLR-337]\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3384-sr_refs = [\"SR-154\"]\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3385-title = \"Single-plan pass gate\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3386-module = \"project-trajectory/scripts/plan_gate.py;project-trajectory/scripts/kitlib/plan_pass.py;project-trajectory/scripts/kitlib/git.py\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3387-code_symbol = \"_own_changes/_close_homes/_regenerated/_is_home/build_paths/binding_problem/_unbound/record_problems/_reviewed_problems/_critique_problems/blocking_ids/_cap_problems/_dismissals/_record_lines/commit_lines/_parents/lane_rider/landing_refusal/_squash_lines/_claim_base/staged_lines/main/plan_dir/plan_path/record_path/critique_path/critique_round/bytes_digest/delta/parse/render/blob/plan_digest/done_when_digest/planmode/gate_rows/_unattributed_squash/lane_commit_walk/staged_heads\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3388-detail = \"The gate reads only rows claimed by the lane's own active folder at the claim base. The closed planmode set is absent, empty, none, single and dual: absent, empty, none and dual are not gated; single is gated; every other normalized value, and a value that is not a string, is held by name. The closed pre-record change set is the record homes and a close: plan records, review records, decision records, session logs, log fragments, the claimed row's own specification, that specification's move to a closed folder with its report and byte-exact inbound-link redirects, or, as a merge's own changes, the compiled change log and the views the trunk regeneration list names; every other own change is build output. Build output is refused unless a parent holds a pass record binding the row, plan digest and Done-when digest left by the change. A changed pass record is accepted only against its first parent when its nine-key grammar is complete, its delta is none or within and is the plan's own line, its digests match the parent's plan and Done-when, its cited critique is byte-identical in that parent, bound to its reviewed commit and accepted by the verdict grammar, and its dispute pair is both present or both empty; a cited critique record is only round one or round two, and any other round is no record. A second-round non-approval additionally requires an accepted dispute dismissal of every blocking and major finding. At filing and commit creation, the reviewed tree also holds the bound plan bytes and Done-when digest. The gate judges the staged lane change, squash-carried lane commits, and landing lane commits oldest first; a squashed tip that no local branch contains is held by name while the landing tree carries any single or out-of-set claim copy; it compares a merge with every parent and holds unreadable claim copies, diffs, listings, records or parents. Trunk and a lane with no single row are not gated. The Done-when digest a record binds is unmoved by a tick or evidence on a Done-when item, so neither unbinds the record. With the trunk undeclared, a branch whose HEAD holds no claim folder is judged at HEAD; any other branch is refused naming the declaration.\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3389-rationale = \"A single-plan item needs one durable, fail-closed release boundary so a skipped hook, rebase, merge or landing cannot turn an unreviewed plan into build output.\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3390-test_refs = \"TC-367\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3391-status = \"Approved\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3392-component = \"CMP-008\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3393-phase = 6\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3394-\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3395-[design.LLR-316]\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3396-sr_refs = [\"SR-237\"]\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3397-title = \"Blackout policy computes the active and most recently ended interval\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3398-module = \"project-trajectory/scripts/agent_policy.py\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3399-code_symbol = \"Blackout/parse_blackout/_utcnow/_windows/blackout_at\"\n--\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml:3745:[design.LLR-362]\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3746-sr_refs = [\"SR-174\"]\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3747-title = \"The shared carrier and reservation record for lane-minted identities\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3748-module = \"project-trajectory/scripts/id_carrier.py;project-trajectory/scripts/trace.py\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3749-code_symbol = \"CARRIER_REF/TRUNK_SPACES/carrier_spaces/parse_reservations/parse_counts/check_work_item/fold/fold_lag/plan_reservation/carrier_tip/carrier_text/write_carrier/landing_lines/render_watermark/bump_watermark/correct_watermark/_mark_history_findings\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3750-detail = \"\"\"The carrier holds the id watermark for every lane-minted space. A reservation moves the carrier by compare-and-swap and appends one record per requested space, stating its inclusive range and work item. Only a reservation writes a record, and only a fold copies one into a watermark. A committed record remains unchanged across every parent. Every watermark writer preserves the records it receives.\"\"\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3751-rationale = \"\"\"Parallel lanes need one allocation authority: ranges chosen from separate bases otherwise collide, and a record that a later writer drops cannot justify either a raised mark or a landing. Compare-and-swap makes a lost race leave no reservation, while preserving records through each writer keeps the authority readable.\"\"\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3752-test_refs = \"TC-401;TC-158\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3753-status = \"Drafted\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3754-component = \"CMP-006\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3755-phase = 6\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3756-\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml:3757:[design.LLR-363]\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3758-sr_refs = [\"SR-174\"]\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3759-title = \"A landing admits only its reserved identities and carries the current fold\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3760-module = \"project-trajectory/scripts/trace.py;project-trajectory/scripts/integrate.py;project-trajectory/scripts/check.py\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3761-code_symbol = \"landing_id_refusal/landing_fold_lag/fold_watermark/_reserved_id_refusal/_landing_ready/_merge_trunk_in/_reserved_ids_mode\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3762-detail = \"\"\"A landing with no added carrier-space identity passes without a reservation. A landing whose added carrier-space identities all lie in records naming its claimed work item passes; an added identity outside such a record, an unreadable claim when identities were added, a missing carrier, or a landing-only record refuses before landing. Each landing carries the fold of the carrier tip it read: the automated landing refreshes a lagging tip, and the hand landing folds its staged watermark and refuses while it still lags. A refresh conflict limited to the watermark resolves to that fold; any other conflict remains refused.\"\"\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3763-rationale = \"\"\"A reservation is authority only when the landing reads it. Folding the carrier's state into both landing routes prevents a valid reservation made after a lane's earlier fold from disappearing at integration, while retaining refusal for claims, records, and conflicts whose authority cannot be established.\"\"\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3764-test_refs = \"TC-402\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3765-status = \"Drafted\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3766-component = \"CMP-008\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3767-phase = 6\nproject-trajectory/scripts/kitlib/git.py:375:def claimed_specs(root, rev, lane=None):\nproject-trajectory/scripts/kitlib/git.py:405:def _listed_blobs(root, rev, paths):\nproject-trajectory/scripts/kitlib/git.py:427:def write_blobs(root, rev, paths, dest):\nproject-trajectory/scripts/kitlib/git.py:456:def lanes_containing(root, tip):\nproject-trajectory/scripts/retire.py:221:def recorded_at(root, rev):\nproject-trajectory/scripts/retire.py:253:def live_ids(root):\nproject-trajectory/scripts/check.py:2052:def _squash_work_items(root, head, tip):\nproject-trajectory/scripts/check.py:2070:def _reserved_ids_refusal(root=\".\"):\ntests/test_id_carrier.py:66:def test_the_grammar_admi